            <ArticleTitle>[In-stent restenosis: which indications for drug-eluting stent?].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>198-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In-stent restenosis remains a limitation of stent implantation. Currently, at the exception of brachytherapy, any percutaneous technique is associated with a high recurrent restenosis rate (&gt; 50%) in diffuse in-stent restenosis. Although based on a small number of patients, eluting stents (sirolimus, paclitaxel) appear promising for the treatment of instent restenosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
